    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Users can tab off the offcanvas panel to reach the amount field and other page controls when the panel is non‑modal, restoring a logical tab order and reducing the number of keystrokes needed to interact with the main form.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "If developers inadvertently rely on the focus trap irrespective of the backdrop setting, changing this behavior could allow focus to leave the offcanvas unexpectedly.",
    "The modal‑related ARIA attributes (aria‑modal=\"true\", role=\"dialog\") are left unchanged; assistive technologies may still perceive the offcanvas as modal when backdrop is false, but the primary tab‑navigation issue is resolved."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "With data-bs-backdrop=\"false\", tabbing from the open-help button reaches the #amount field within 6 Tab presses.",
    "With the default backdrop (true), focus remains trapped inside the offcanvas and cannot escape to #amount without explicitly closing it.",
    "Keyboard closing via the Escape key continues to work when keyboard:true.",
    "Panel open/close animations, visibility changes, and ARIA attribute updates remain as originally implemented."
  ]
}

